  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kragujevac District Heating Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of a sovereign loan of up to EUR 18 million to the Republic of Serbia  (the &quot;Client&quot;) consisting of 2 tranches. The loan proceeds of Tranche 1 (EUR 15  million) will be used for: 1) decommissioning of old coal boilers from the  district heating (&quot;DH&quot;) system in the city of Kragujevac (the &quot;City&quot;), 2)  installation of new natural gas based hot water boilers, with a total capacity  of 110MW, and 3) project supervision. The loan proceeds of Tranche 2 (EUR 3  million) will be used for: i) rehabilitation of the ash disposal site, and ii)  related procurement and implementation support, and works supervision.  The Project will enable the full elimination of coal from the City&apos;s district  heating system and will significantly improve the air quality of the city due  to the central location of the coal boilers being replaced. The Project will  serve as a foundation for future investments in introducing renewable energy  sources and energy efficiency measures, which will be assessed through the  TC-funded support. The Tranche 2 investment will support the remediation of the  ash disposal site located within the complex of District Heating Company (&quot; Energetika&quot;), which is the source of major environmental risk in the City. The  Project will improve the air quality by eliminating sulphur oxides and  particulate matter emissions and significantly reducing nitrous oxide  emissions.</narrative>
  </description>
